          "summary": "CNN legal expert Ryan Goodman said Monday that federal law “could not be clearer” when it comes to President Donald Trump using taxpayer dollars for campaign-style advertisements promoting himself weeks before the crucial midterm elections. CNN’s Erin Burnett asked Goodman, an NYU law professor and former special counsel for the Department of Defense, whether there was “any question” about the legality of White House employees using government resources to produce the ads . “There’s not,” Goodman said…",
